## 3 Key Insights From This Data

---

**Insight 1 — Data Availability**
> "Chicago crash data is fully reliable only from 2016 onwards. Before 2015 the data is incomplete — only 2 and 6 records show the digitization was just beginning."

---

**Insight 2 — COVID Impact**
> "2020 clearly shows COVID lockdown effect — dropped from 116,751 in 2019 to 91,472 in 2020. That's 25,000 less crashes — directly because of reduced traffic during lockdown."

---

**Insight 3 — 2018 Was Worst Year**
> "2018 had the highest crashes — 118,343. Could indicate more vehicles, road conditions, or population growth that year."

